    <string name="studio_help_button">?</string>
    <string name="studio_help_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="studio_help_text">Spread · Choose a drum in Notes, or hold a hit in Rhythm. Set the number of hits per bar and their offset. Listen, then apply to the visible patterns. Undo restores the lane.\n\nDynamic touch · On the Notes keyboard, touch near the top of a key for a soft attack or near the bottom for a stronger one. Dynamic touch is on by default. You can switch it off in Studio settings. Recording also captures MIDI velocity and sustain pedal holds.\n\nPanels · Drag the top handle to make room for the keyboard. The cross closes a panel.\n\nNotes · Slide on the keys at the left to change register silently. The arrows at the top left jump to notes outside the screen. The keyboard opens at C4. The marked key is the note for a new Rhythm step. In the Notes panel, Octave sets that note for the selected track (octave 4 by default) and moves the keyboard there. On a melodic pad, tap the track name for Notes or the instrument name beside it for Sound. Each track has its own octave. Key and scale apply to the song. In Clean, Filter and Drive, the playable keys are lit. On Filter and Drive, slide vertically to shape a held note. On Pads, the left edge of that track’s tile starts on the same note in both keyboard and theremin modes. Existing notes keep their pitch. Hold the Notes button to fit the pattern or switch between one and two octaves. Drag the body of a note to move it or its right edge to resize it.\n\nRhythm: tap the squares to place drum hits. Press and hold a lit square to set its strength, length and pitch. Select outlines steps or notes to copy, cut, paste or delete.\n\nNotes: pick a track in the top row. A track that plays notes shows the grid and the keyboard: draw notes, or play and press Record while the music runs. A drum track shows its sound: three versions, pitch, length, or a kit from your soundfont.\n\nMixer: one strip per track with its volume. Mute silences it, Solo keeps only that track, Effects opens balance, reverb, echo, filter, distortion and lo-fi. The pad controls the filter and reverb. Turn on Hold to keep its position throughout the song. Turn it off to hear pattern gestures again. Record my gesture records movement into the loop.\n\nPatterns A to D hold four different loops. Song plays them one after another. Export saves an audio file, a MIDI file, or sends the sound to the audio editor.\n\nMy sound: record two seconds with the microphone; it replaces the sound of the Perc. track.\n\nPads · A to D select a loop. During playback it starts at the end of the current loop. Tap the queued letter again to cancel. Finish recording before switching loops. Arrange lets you drag instruments and tap ×0.5 for a compact tile or the arrow for a wide tile. Tap the active control again to restore normal size. Tap Arrange again to play. Sounds opens instruments and track effects. The XY pad controls the whole mix. Big squares to play the drums with your fingers. Tap the mode in the header of a melodic pad. On the keyboard, slide vertically to add drive or close the filter. Clean keeps the track tone. On the theremin, slide between scale notes and move up for a louder, brighter sound. Recording captures the notes you play; vertical modulation is live. Roll: keep a finger on a drum to repeat it in time. Record starts after one bar of clicks.\n\nTheremin: slide your finger to play; left and right change the note (always on the scale), up makes the sound louder and brighter.\n\nSound > Record a sound: sing or play a note, the synth plays it on every key. Keep this sound finds it again in every song.</string>
