    <string-array name="studio_lexicon_defs"><item>How loud the track is.</item><item>Places the sound more to the left or to the right.</item><item>Silences the track.</item><item>Keeps only this track.</item><item>The sound rings out as if in a big room.</item><item>The sound repeats and fades away.</item><item>Muffles the sound (to the left) or thins it (to the right).</item><item>Makes the sound rougher and louder.</item><item>A grain like an old machine or a worn tape.</item><item>While your finger is on it, the filter (left to right) and the reverb (bottom to top) change for the whole song.</item><item>Makes a drum sound lower or higher.</item><item>How long the sound lasts before it fades.</item><item>A set of notes, such as C, D, E, F, G, A and B in C major. On the scale limits playing and entering notes in Notes to this set. Melodic pads always follow the chosen scale.</item><item>The note the scale starts from.</item><item>Plays the notes of a chord one after another.</item><item>One of the four loops, A to D.</item><item>The speed, in beats per minute.</item><item>A file of recorded instruments (piano, guitar, drums…).</item><item>The next steps you place on this track take the strength, length and pitch of this one.</item><item>Outline steps, then tap Copy or Cut. Move the dashed preview on the grid, check the track and step, then tap Paste here. Cancel leaves a copy on the clipboard. Undo restores a cut.</item><item>The track dips at each kick drum hit, then comes back: the sound breathes with the beat.</item><item>Turn on Roll, pick a rate and hold a drum pad.</item><item>Studio lets you shape the sound. SCC and Famicom play instruments from the GXSCC banks by GASHISOFT. Switch banks while the loop plays to compare them. Tap the instrument name to browse families, or use − and + to step through sounds.</item><item>Smooth bass rounds off the upper harmonics of SCC and Famicom notes below C4. The note keeps its pitch.</item><item>@string/studio_fm_help</item></string-array>
